{"id":"e12t1","name":"7-Day Rolling Revenue per Store","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["sales_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A retail chain wants to smooth its daily sales curves. For every store and every day with sales, compute the revenue over the last 7 calendar days.</p>\n<h3>Input</h3>\n<p><code>sales_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>store_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>sale_date</td>\n<td>date</td>\n<td>never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>amount</td>\n<td>double</td>\n<td>sale amount; may be null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>A store can have several rows on the same day, and no row at all on some days.</p>\n<h3>Rules</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Rows with a null <code>amount</code> are ignored. A (store, day) appears in the output only if the store has at least one row with a non-null <code>amount</code> on that day.</li>\n<li><code>daily_revenue</code> is the sum of the amounts of the store on that day.</li>\n<li>The 7-day window of day D covers the calendar days from D - 6 to D, both inclusive, whatever the number of days with sales in between.</li>\n<li><code>rolling_7d_revenue</code> is the sum of <code>daily_revenue</code> over the window. <code>rolling_7d_avg</code> is <code>rolling_7d_revenue / 7</code> (always divided by 7 calendar days).</li>\n<li><code>days_with_sales_7d</code> is the number of days of the window that appear in the output for this store.</li>\n<li>All doubles are rounded to 2 decimals.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Output</h3>\n<p>One row per (store, day with sales), with exactly these columns, in this order:</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>store_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>sale_date</td>\n<td>date</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>daily_revenue</td>\n<td>double</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>rolling_7d_revenue</td>\n<td>double</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>rolling_7d_avg</td>\n<td>double</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>days_with_sales_7d</td>\n<td>long</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows are sorted by <code>store_id</code> ascending, then <code>sale_date</code> ascending.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>sales_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>store_id</th>\n<th>sale_date</th>\n<th>amount</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-01</td>\n<td>100.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-01</td>\n<td>50.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-02</td>\n<td>null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-03</td>\n<td>30.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-07</td>\n<td>20.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>B</td>\n<td>2024-03-05</td>\n<td>7.5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-08</td>\n<td>10.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-10</td>\n<td>5.0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expected output</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>store_id</th>\n<th>sale_date</th>\n<th>daily_revenue</th>\n<th>rolling_7d_revenue</th>\n<th>rolling_7d_avg</th>\n<th>days_with_sales_7d</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-01</td>\n<td>150.0</td>\n<td>150.0</td>\n<td>21.43</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-03</td>\n<td>30.0</td>\n<td>180.0</td>\n<td>25.71</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-07</td>\n<td>20.0</td>\n<td>200.0</td>\n<td>28.57</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-08</td>\n<td>10.0</td>\n<td>60.0</td>\n<td>8.57</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>2024-03-10</td>\n<td>5.0</td>\n<td>35.0</td>\n<td>5.0</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>B</td>\n<td>2024-03-05</td>\n<td>7.5</td>\n<td>7.5</td>\n<td>1.07</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>On 2024-03-08 the window covers 2024-03-02 to 2024-03-08, so the sales of 2024-03-01 are no longer included.</p>\n<h3>Function signature</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">from pyspark.sql import DataFrame\n\ndef solve(sales_df: DataFrame) -&gt; DataFrame:\n    ...\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Constraints</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the PySpark DataFrame API. Do not convert to pandas, do not call <code>collect()</code> or <code>toPandas()</code> inside <code>solve</code>, do not use Python UDFs.</li>\n<li><code>sales_df</code> has up to 10^7 rows, for up to 10^4 stores.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import DataFrame, Window\nfrom pyspark.sql import functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(sales_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return sales_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":[],"minutes":22,"source":"Examen d'entraînement d'octobre n°4, question 1","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"sales_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"store_id string, sale_date date, amount double","rows":[["A","2024-03-01",100.0],["A","2024-03-01",50.0],["A","2024-03-02",null],["A","2024-03-03",30.0],["A","2024-03-07",20.0],["B","2024-03-05",7.5],["A","2024-03-08",10.0],["A","2024-03-10",5.0]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["store_id","sale_date","daily_revenue","rolling_7d_revenue","rolling_7d_avg","days_with_sales_7d"],"rows":[["A","2024-03-01",150.0,150.0,21.43,1],["A","2024-03-03",30.0,180.0,25.71,2],["A","2024-03-07",20.0,200.0,28.57,3],["A","2024-03-08",10.0,60.0,8.57,3],["A","2024-03-10",5.0,35.0,5.0,3],["B","2024-03-05",7.5,7.5,1.07,1]]}}],"hidden_n":4,"hidden":"","solution":""}